Okay, here's the story:

Fizzwick, a Gnome Warlock barely taller than a worg, puffed as he trudged through Stranglethorn Vale. His Succubus, Lilith, floated beside him, occasionally batting at the oversized mosquitos. "Honestly, Lilith," Fizzwick grumbled, "couldn't you charm one of those trolls to carry me? My little legs are killing me!" Lilith just smirked, her tail swaying. They were on a quest to collect raptor eggs, and Fizzwick was already regretting his choice of location. Suddenly, a group of hostile panthers pounced. Fizzwick yelped, but Lilith, with a seductive whisper, turned the panthers against each other. Fizzwick, relieved, continued his quest, muttering about the benefits of having a charming companion.

Answer:

Succubus's Seduction ability can be used on players.
 [end of text]


